{% comment %}
  Step 3 (shown as "Step 2 of 5") — doctor selection. Now reached from the
  new Concern Select step, not directly from Entry — see that step's own
  comment for why.

  MOBILE REDESIGN per a later Figma pass (node 544:3781), reverting the
  prior backend-integration work on this screen — explicit instruction:
  - The facility strip (4 clinics, picking which one's doctors to fetch)
    is gone. The design shows no in-page clinic picker on this screen at
    all, just the shared header's facility badge (see
    kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid) — the CMS facility-strip/
    GET /api/public/doctors?facility_id=X wiring this replaced is removed
    from kal-booking-flow.js too (setFacility, loadDoctorsForFacility,
    renderDoctorCards, MOCK_DOCTORS, the data-kal-facility and
    data-kal-doctor-option click handlers).
  - The doctor card is a full static mockup again (name, degree,
    languages, experience, specialty tags, next slot, price) — see
    kal-booking-flow-doctor-card.liquid's own comment for why this
    intentionally shows content the real API doesn't provide yet.
  - Downstream steps (Slot Picker) aren't affected: they already read
    their own hardcoded default data-kal-doctor-id/data-kal-facility-id
    off .kal-step-slot-picker's root element (see that step's own
    liquid), never actually depending on doctorSelect's old dynamic
    selection state.

  Single shared markup, not a __mobile + __desktop split — see the "SHARED
  STEP SHELL" comment in kal-booking-flow.css for why and how the layout
  switches at 750px. Left column reuses .kal-step-entry__info exactly like
  every other step's desktop composition (per the Figma spec — only the
  heading text differs); this pass is mobile-only, so its copy ("Who would
  you like to see?") is left as-is while the mobile intro heading below
  gets the new copy.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-doctor-select kal-step-shell">

  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info">
    <div class="kal-step-entry__info-content">
      <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading">Who would you like to see?</h2>
      <p class="kal-step-entry__body-text">
        Book a consultation in under a minute in-clinic or video. Confirmation
        arrives instantly, no account required.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-step-entry__location">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
        <!-- ICON: location-pin (not received yet) -->
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__location-text">
        Kerala Ayurveda Wellness Center, Indiranagar &middot; Opens 8 AM
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    {%- comment -%}
      Per the updated Figma spec (node 544:3781), Doctor Select's header
      is the exact same composition Concern Select uses — back button,
      mobile facility badge / desktop progress dots, close button, plus a
      mobile step progress bar underneath. Shared via the same snippet
      rather than duplicating that markup here (see
      kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid); the old dots-only header
      (with its own inline "2/5" text and no facility badge/step-bar) is
      gone.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-header', back_target: 'concern-select', step_number: 2, step_total: 5, next_label: 'Date & Time' -%}

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
        <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Choose your doctor</h2>
        <p class="kal-step-doctor-select__subtext">Select a doctor and how you&rsquo;d like to consult</p>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-toggle-group">
        <button type="button" class="kal-toggle-btn kal-toggle-btn--active" data-kal-mode="in-clinic">
          <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'mode-location' -%}
          </span>
          In-Clinic
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="kal-toggle-btn" data-kal-mode="video">
          <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--video">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'mode-online' -%}
          </span>
          Video Consult
        </button>
      </div>

      {%- assign doctor_photo_url = 'kal-doctor-photo-placeholder.jpg' | asset_url -%}
      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__list">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-doctor-card',
          name: 'Dr. Neethu Jayachandran',
          degree: 'BAMS',
          languages: 'English &middot; Hindi &middot; Malayalam',
          experience: '12 yrs experience',
          tags: 'Anxiety,Stress Management,Diabetes Care,Preventive Health',
          next_slot: 'Today, 10:30 AM',
          price: '&#8377;500',
          selected: true,
          photo_url: doctor_photo_url
        -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="slot-picker">
        Continue
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>
